Elven gear doesn't really work with itself very well, other than the 
enchantment limits.

So why not make elven gear synergic and gently nudge the elves away from 
iron.

Anytime an elf character wields or wears iron they would get an annoying 
message like "The touch of iron offends your elven sense of style" and 
knocked for an alignment point.  Yeah, it's noise in the late game, but 
early on it hurts.

Elven boots and cloak are redundant so change the cloak to granting free 
action and remove sleep resistance from the racial ability slot.  The 
elven leather helm can then grant animal empathy, which would just make 
animals react to the wearer as if they were the same alignment.  If you 
are wearing all three items you get invisibility.

Finally an elven cloak would act like a robe, but only when worn over an 
elven mithril coat (which would otherwise be redundant for the ### 
resistance).

Elven wizards would start with an elven cloak instead of the CoMR and 
their clerics would also start with elven cloak and quarterstaff.

Switch their skills around a bit to avoid the iron weapons and favor the 
elven weapon types in the game and for their sac gifts they are never 
given iron and their first sac gift is always some elven wooden practice 
blade.

Stormbringer and Magicbane would be moved to "unknown metal" to avoid 
triggering the iron restriction and would be the second sac gifts for 
elven rangers and wizards respectively.

